# GnuChanTerm's own terminfo entry.
#
# A terminal's name is a promise, and this file is the promise written down.
# Programs do not read escape sequences out of a manual; they look the name up
# in this database and use what it says. A name with no entry resolves to
# `dumb` -- no colour, no cursor addressing, no screen handling -- and a
# program that gets `dumb` behaves as if the terminal were a printer. A shell
# in that state cannot even redraw a line it is editing, which is why a
# terminal with a name it cannot resolve looks broken rather than plain.
#
# SYNTAX, WHICH THIS FILE GOT WRONG
#
# `#` does NOT begin a comment inside a capability list. In this format `#`
# introduces a NUMBER -- `colors#256` is the number 256 -- so a capability
# followed by `# a note` is read as the capability, the number marker, and then
# `a` as the start of a value, and the compiler stops with "Illegal character".
#
# Comments are whole lines and start with `#` in column one. Nothing below
# carries a note on the same line as a capability; every explanation is here,
# above it. That is the rule this file broke, and it is why the entry had never
# once been installed: `tic` refused the source, `gcl-256color` resolved to
# nothing, and every program that read it fell back to a dumb terminal.
#
# WHAT IS CLAIMED, AND WHAT IS NOT
#
# Only what term_vt.c actually implements. A capability claimed here and not
# implemented is a program sending a sequence into a terminal that ignores it,
# which shows as a wrong screen rather than as an error, so the safe direction
# is to claim less.
#
# NOT claimed, and why:
#
#   ccc / initc        OSC 4 is consumed and not acted on; colours are fixed
#   flash              `?5` (reverse video) is not implemented
#   mc0 / mc4 / mc5    there is no printer
#   oc                 there is no origin mode
#   rep                `CSI b` (repeat) is not in the parser
#   cbt                `CSI Z` is not in the parser
#   tsl / fsl          OSC 0 is consumed and the window title is not changed
#   OSC 52 clipboard   not implemented
#   SIXEL / ReGIS      not implemented

